  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Mainstreaming Biodiversity Conservation and Sustainable Land Management (SLM) into Development Planning: Making Environmental Land Use Planning (ELUP) Operational in Argentina</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Generate multiple biodiversity and land degradation benefits by developing a system of policy, economic, financial and technical instruments and governance mechanisms for environmental land use planning (ELUP) to mainstream socioeconomic and environmental evaluation of ecosystem goods and services (ESG) in decision making at different government levels and sectors.</narrative>
  </description>
